# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_seat_metering.py" "SEAT METERING GATE: PASS" "seat metering (human vs bot)" "seat metering (the founder's seat/MRR line meters REAL HUMANS, not a structural \$0): a HUMAN PR/landing author (act_for_claim / record_landing) is provisioned agent_kind='human' so core._seat_count(30) counts it [was DEFAULT 'ai' on main -> a STRUCTURAL 0 for every tenant]; a BOT author [the webhook's pull_request.user.type=='Bot' / a push sender.type=='Bot' -> the gate's p_author_is_bot flag, since the '[bot]' login marker is STRIPPED before storage and can't be recovered] is stamped 'ai' and EXCLUDED [the AI-fleet wedge: bots are free]; SELF-HEAL corrects an author stored under the OLD 'ai' default to 'human' on its next claim [no migration; a bot stays 'ai', no false flip]; owner_cost_surface() reflects the real seat count [the measured 0->N: active_agents/paid_seats]; the App/seat agents AG-* are NEVER flipped [only 'GH-' author rows self-heal]; content-free [a boolean, never PII]" "seat metering: humans become seats, bots stay free, the founder's MRR is no longer \$0 (load-bearing: RED on origin/main where every author is 'ai'/seat_count=0, GREEN after the fix)" 24
